    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0423" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.429/905: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-12T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 12—10:08
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>815. My 768 of September 22, noon, and previous telegrams,<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d266-f1"/> I have just received a note from the Foreign Office
                    stating that they <pb facs="0424" n="300" xml:id="pg300"/> prefer that the
                    matter be handled direct with the Dominion Government through the British
                    Embassy at Washington.</p>
                <p>I am mailing copies of the note<anchor n="15a" xml:id="d266-f2"/> in the next
                    pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
